{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Clouds</b> — The clouds are so called because they are lifted from the edge of the earth, and the wind carries them." "<b>but no rain</b> — In the clouds, to cause rain to fall." "<b>so is a man</b> — who lies and deceives, that he should give though he has nothing at all — compared to the clouds, and it is not proper to do so."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:38.275842496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}